From 1194d2acae3fec72f370b0c161fcc1a48a81e9a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:48:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] velox: optionally prefetch ASG commands while RenderThread
 decodes (patch 0018)

VELOX_ASG_PREFETCH=1 makes the serial receive path (now readRing) write
into host-private chunks framed on packet boundaries. RenderThread decodes
published packets in place (no second copy; the 0009 borrow still only sees
host memory). A prefetch thread reads ahead while RenderThread decodes a
large view (VELOX_ASG_PREFETCH_AHEAD=2, MIN_KB=64) and polls an empty ring
sparsely (POLL=1024 pauses); when RenderThread runs out of packets it takes
the rings over and receives directly, so small synchronous round trips do
not pay a thread hand-off (and skip all signalling when the rings are free).
One reader owns the rings at a time, so the ring order, host_state handling,
replies and all length/range/opcode checks are unchanged. waitForFinished
joins the prefetch thread before the ASG context frees the rings. Disabled
after a snapshot load; disabled behaviour is the previous readRaw.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
